# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT-0
# HakiOS fragment: the Pixel 10 with Google's UFS host, READ ONLY. The one thing this phone's first image leaves out and this one
# puts back: the kernel's own UFS driver (hakios.ufshc.c, ufs_native_soc=lga) reads the GPT of the phone's first logical unit and
# makes /dev/ufs_NAME of each partition, so that init can mount the system image off `userdata` (system_apfs=ufs_userdata)
# as the Galaxy S9's does off its own partition. The driver refuses every write for this SoC, whatever a boot argument says, and
# mkimage.sh -U's audit (audit-image.py --ufs-ro) refuses an image whose command line asks for one.
CONFIG_HAKIOS_UFS=y
